<title>CHILE: Chile cenbank raises 1997 copper price forecast.</title>
<headline>Chile cenbank raises 1997 copper price forecast.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's Central Bank has raised its forecast of average copper prices this year to $1 per lb from $0.95 estimated in the national budget in September, said president Carlos Massad.</p>
<p>Chile, the world's largest copper producer, traditionally takes a conservative view on possible increases in world copper prices.</p>
<p>((-- Paulina Modiano, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
